.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payouts-report-hash - Report a transfer you broadcast yourself


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payouts report-hash   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Tell the gateway the hash of a payout transfer you signed and broadcast yourself
(a wallet that signs and sends in one step), instead of 'payouts submit'.

.PP
The hash must be THIS transfer — from the wallet, to the token, this amount to
this destination: a hash a node already knows that is anything else is refused
(foreign_transfer_hash), and one another payout records is 409 payout_hash_in_use.
A hash no node has seen yet is accepted and settled from its receipt.

.PP
Also the way back for a payout that failed submission_timeout or dropped because
the transaction that went out was sped up or replaced: report its hash and the
payout returns to submitted.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for report-hash


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payouts report-hash <payout_id> 0x5c50…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payouts(1)\fP
